--- A checked index or range is outside its valid extent.
---
--- Compiler-check reasons. The representation is the ordinary nonzero
--- atom carrier; callers compare identities, never assumed integer codes.
public out_of_range: atom
--- A checked arithmetic operation cannot represent its result.
public overflow: atom
--- A checked conversion cannot represent the source value in its target type.
public bad_conversion: atom
--- Execution reached a path declared unreachable.
public unreachable: atom
--- The compiler's four panic atoms. A program may supply the specified
--- nonreturning panic handler; these failures are not allocator error
--- returns.
public panic_kind: type = out_of_range | overflow | bad_conversion | unreachable
